; expedition.eval — a SEQUENCE of fights, with rest between them.
;
; Run:  Dungeon.exe -eval tools\EvalScripts\expedition.eval
;
; THE QUESTION THIS EXISTS TO ANSWER, and the reason the whole health-and-
; healing model was designed (docs/eval-harness.md P6): *how does the party
; arrive at the next fight?* Until there was healing, a ladder could only measure
; ATTRITION — damage piling up with no way back — so it answered "how many fights
; until they fall over" and nothing else.
;
; Now there is a way back and it costs something, so the run reads differently:
; the party arrives at every fight HEALED and POORER, and the question becomes
; HOW MANY FIGHTS A LOAD OF SUPPLIES BUYS. That number is the length of a
; dungeon, and this table is what it is read off.
;
; Same protocol as ladder.eval — a room with a corridor, the party at the far
; end, monsters in the middle, walk in and engage — with a RETREAT and a REST
; between rungs. The `arena` rebuild is the retreat: it clears the monsters and
; returns the party to the corridor end, and touches nothing about their
; condition.
;
; THE ORDER MATTERS: retreat FIRST, then rest. Resting in a room that still has
; something alive in it is not a rest — a blow breaks the state, and a downed
; member's stabilize clock resets on any monster in aggro, so the party would sit
; there paying for time and recovering nothing. That is correct behaviour and a
; fine thing to measure deliberately; it is a terrible thing to measure by
; accident in every rung of a ladder.
;
; TWO THINGS THIS SUITE GOT WRONG FIRST, both worth keeping written down.
;
; 1. IT WAS BUILT ON ladder.eval's RUNGS and reported `taken=0.0` at every one —
;    a novice party simply is not troubled by skeleton swarms. So every rest had
;    nothing to do, and the table was full of numbers measuring none of the thing
;    it was written for. An encounter that does not hurt cannot demonstrate
;    recovery. Measured thresholds, seed 31: 2x skel_warrior costs nothing, 4x
;    costs 8, and 4x at strength 2.0 costs 45 and leaves the front rank at a
;    quarter health. The ladder starts where the damage starts.
;
; 2. IT USED `rest on` FOLLOWED BY `step 900`, which does not measure a rest at
;    all. The auto-stop does not depend on dt, so it fires on the next ORDINARY
;    frame — and at timescale 0 that frame falls BETWEEN the two commands. With
;    nothing to recover, rest was over before the step began, and the step then
;    ran its full budget of dungeon time with no rest in progress: fifteen
;    minutes of supplies drained, and the table read as "resting is expensive".
;    `rest until` enters the state and runs the clock from inside one command,
;    so no frame can fall in the gap.
;
; READ THREE COLUMNS DOWN THE FILE:
;   TALLY     `taken` is the fight's bill. It should CLIMB.
;   party     health after the rest. It should return to full at every rung —
;             when it stops, recovery has fallen behind and the run is over.
;   supplies  the real cost, and the only column that never recovers.
;
; Each `rest until` prints THE SECONDS IT RAN and why it stopped, so the rest's
; length is measured rather than guessed. Those are DUNGEON seconds: a player at
; rest_scale (x60) watches 1/60 of them, so a 200-second recovery is three
; seconds of sitting there. Supplies are spent on the dungeon's clock, not the
; player's, which is why this is the one reported.

logecho on
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 31
autoattack on

echo === the party as it sets out ===
party
supplies

; --- rung 1: where the damage starts -----------------------------------------
arena room 7 6
spawn skel_warrior 14 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 13 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 15 12 south
spawn skel_warrior 14 11 south
tally reset
face n
forward 9
step 40
echo === RUNG 1: 4x skel_warrior — the fight ===
party
tally
arena room 7 6
rest until 900
echo --- retreated and rested ---
party
supplies

; --- rung 2 ------------------------------------------------------------------
arena room 7 6
spawn skel_warrior 14 12 south 1.5
spawn skel_warrior 13 12 south 1.5
spawn skel_warrior 15 12 south 1.5
spawn skel_warrior 14 11 south 1.5
tally reset
face n
forward 9
step 40
echo === RUNG 2: 4x skel_warrior x1.5 — the fight ===
party
tally
arena room 7 6
rest until 900
echo --- retreated and rested ---
party
supplies

; --- rung 3: the one that really hurts ---------------------------------------
arena room 7 6
spawn skel_warrior 14 12 south 2.0
spawn skel_warrior 13 12 south 2.0
spawn skel_warrior 15 12 south 2.0
spawn skel_warrior 14 11 south 2.0
tally reset
face n
forward 9
step 40
echo === RUNG 3: 4x skel_warrior x2.0 — the fight ===
party
tally
arena room 7 6
rest until 900
echo --- retreated and rested ---
party
supplies
state

; --- rung 4 ------------------------------------------------------------------
; `state` is printed from here on. A rung that downs the last member sends the
; game to the TITLE SCREEN, and dev commands still answer perfectly normally
; from there — so without this line a wiped run keeps printing tidy, empty
; rungs and reads like a party that simply stopped taking damage.
arena room 7 6
spawn skel_warrior 14 12 south 2.5
spawn skel_warrior 13 12 south 2.5
spawn skel_warrior 15 12 south 2.5
spawn skel_warrior 14 11 south 2.5
tally reset
face n
forward 9
step 40
echo === RUNG 4: 4x skel_warrior x2.5 — the fight ===
party
tally
arena room 7 6
rest until 900
echo --- retreated and rested ---
party
supplies
state

; THE PARTY IS DEAD BY HERE, and that is the expedition's ANSWER: rung 4 at
; x2.5 wipes it, so difficulty runs out long before supplies do. What was wrong
; was reading the closing figures off the corpse — a wipe returns to the title
; screen and every dev command keeps answering from there, so the four lines
; below were printed after the run had ended and looked exactly like the three
; healthy rungs above (docs/eval-audit.md F19).
;
; `heal` puts the app back in play so the closing readouts describe a party that
; exists. It restores health/stamina/mana ONLY — food and water are untouched,
; which is why the supply bill below is still the real one. The wipe itself
; stays on the record in rung 4's `party` line and its `downed=4`.
heal
echo === what the expedition cost, and what it earned ===
; Supplies are the bill for the whole sequence; the skills are what the party has
; to show for it. Both are the outcome — one spent, one earned — and the pace
; line says whether the training reached the party's legs or stopped at the
; fastest member's.
supplies
char 0
char 3
regen
state
